\subsection{LSTM Deep Learning Model}

While the heuristic model provides interpretability, it lacks the capacity to capture complex nonlinear relationships and long-range temporal dependencies inherent in network traffic patterns. To address these limitations, we adopt a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) based deep learning architecture that automatically learns temporal patterns from raw sequences.

LSTM networks are particularly well-suited for capacity constraint prediction, as network bottlenecks typically develop gradually over extended time horizons. The sequential nature of LSTMs enables the model to maintain long-term memory of past network states while filtering transient noise through gating mechanisms. Our architecture, detailed in Table~\ref{tab}, employs a two-layer design with fully connected layers for final classification.

