\subsubsection{Ground Truth Definition}
\label{groundtruth}
To evaluate prediction accuracy, we define the ground truth based on buffer occupancy. When the offered traffic exceeds the available capacity, excess packets are queued, resulting in persistent buffer buildup-a clear signal of congestion. To filter out short-term fluctuations and identify sustained saturation, a threshold of 100 packets is applied; any time interval during which buffer occupancy exceeds this value is labeled as `1', indicating a capacity-limited state.

