\subsection{Qualitative Results}

Fig.~\ref{fig} presents a sample test case illustrating the performance of the heuristic model with and without the application of a median filter. As shown in Fig.~\ref{fig}(a), the raw input signal without filtering exhibits bursty traffic artifacts, which obscure the long-term network peak trend and result in poor detection performance. These short-term noisy spikes distort the model's perception of the peak traffic threshold, elevating the tolerance zone and thereby suppressing the detection of genuine congestion events.
In contrast, Fig.~\ref{fig}(b) demonstrates that applying a median filter effectively removes high-frequency noise, allowing the model to better identify sustained periods of congestion. However, the filtered model remains susceptible to false positives, such as the anomaly observed in the final 50 seconds of the sequence. This behavior underscores the heuristic model’s sensitivity to input noise and its reliance on careful parameter tuning for optimal performance.

