\section{Conclusion}

This paper addressed the challenge of detecting persistent capacity limitations that manifest as sustained throughput plateaus, often overlooked by traditional congestion control mechanisms. Such plateaus serve as indicators of user-level bandwidth saturation and enable estimation of the maximum achievable throughput, providing a more accurate reflection of achievable performance than nominal plan rates.

To detect these conditions, we proposed a hybrid framework that combines heuristic peak detection with LSTM-based temporal modeling enhanced by Elastic Weight Consolidation (EWC). The framework achieved 92.1% accuracy and an 81.5% F1-score under controlled streaming scenarios, outperforming baseline machine learning methods by 13 percentage points in F1-score while maintaining interpretability. By reliably estimating maximum achievable throughput, the framework provides actionable insights for proactive bandwidth management, QoE optimization, and user-informed decisions such as upgrading to higher-tier network plans. Future work will explore real-time deployment and integration with automated network management systems.





